## MODULE 07 — Multi-Platform Publishing Engine

This must be a reliable independent backend service.

### Publishing workflow

Each platform should have its own publishing job.

For example:

One video is scheduled for four platforms.

- YouTube succeeds.
- Facebook succeeds.
- Instagram fails.
- TikTok is waiting for authorization.

The system must record four independent results.

A failure on one platform must not cancel successful publications on the others.

### Features
- Independent publishing queues.
- API response validation.
- Publishing status tracking.
- Automatic retry.
- Exponential backoff.
- Error classification.
- Duplicate publication prevention.
- Rate-limit handling.
- Token expiration handling.
- Publication verification.
- Post URL storage.
- Publishing history.

### Publishing statuses

- Pending.
- Queued.
- Processing.
- Uploading.
- Publishing.
- Published.
- Partially published.
- Failed.
- Requires authorization.
- Requires manual action.

Never mark a video as published simply because an API request was sent. Verify the actual publication result where the platform provides confirmation.

